  "body": "## What changed\n\nOne local eikonal pass re-normalises the stock view's narrow band before the render.\n\n- New `FieldLattice::renormalize()` in `stock_sim/preview/eikonal.rs`. It's one round of fast sweeping (Zhao, Math. Comp. 2005; also Sussman–Smereka–Osher and Russo–Smereka): the eikonal update applied once in each of the 8 sweep orders, over band texels only.\n- It's called in `PackedBase::of` (`app/src/stock_view.rs`) before the GPU upload. A refusal is logged and the lattice is used as it was.\n- The surface stays put:\n  - texels next to an opposite-sign texel are frozen, bit for bit;\n  - every other texel keeps its sign and never reaches 0;\n  - texels at or past `cap` are untouched, and new values are capped at `cap`.\n- Only the mesh layer is rewritten; the cut layer is unchanged, so later playback frames stay sign-correct.\n- Display only: the verdict paths (`march`, `deviate_field`) still read the sparse field. The CPU `preview()` is unchanged.\n- Cost: one classification pass, then 8 updates per band texel. It's deterministic, and bounded by the 8M-texel pack limit; the CSG test froze 3,837 and solved 15,211 texels.\n\n## Pins (`crates/sim/tests/stock_eikonal.rs`, 6, plus a unit test)\n\n- After cuts (cylinder pocket, ball slot, flat slot): mean ||∇φ|−1| drops from 0.367 to 0.048 (bound < 0.08), and texels within 0.1 of a unit gradient rise from 2% to 83%. A second round changes nothing.\n- Every sign is kept, and every zero-crossing edge's ends are bit-identical.\n- The cylinder pocket is within 0.21 of the exact distance at a 0.5 cell. Under the uncut top face the field reads exactly 5 − z.\n- Out-of-band texels are untouched, the cut layer is unchanged, nothing exceeds `cap`, and results are deterministic. A malformed lattice is refused.\n\n## Readings\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-sim` all green except overhang_laws (3), which fails identically on main (#202). app stock_view 4 and stock_play 7 pass; clippy on sim and app is clean; no snapshot changed.\n\nChangelog: The stock view's narrow band is re-normalized by one eikonal (fast-sweeping) pass before the render, so shading reads a true distance gradient; sign and surface unchanged\n\nFixes #22\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
